    "references": [
      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT4-109#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT4-109 (Mar. 28, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it does. Even if the Digimon's original DP is less than 16000, if it becomes 16000 or greater after getting +3000 DP from this card's effect, it gains ＜Blocker＞, ＜Reboot＞, and ＜Security A. +1＞.",
        "question": "I use this card's effect to give a Digimon +3000 DP. If that Digimon now has 16000 DP or more, does it gain ＜Blocker＞, ＜Reboot＞, and ＜Security A. +1＞?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No. Once the Digimon meets the conditions to gain ＜Blocker＞, ＜Reboot＞, and ＜Security A. +1＞, it keeps them until the end of your opponent's next turn, even if its DP is reduced to 15000 or less.",
        "question": "I use this card's effect to give one of my Digimon ＜Blocker＞, ＜Reboot＞, and ＜Security A. +1＞. If another effect reduces that Digimon to 15000 or less, does it lose ＜Blocker＞, ＜Reboot＞, and ＜Security A. +1＞?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, it doesn't. The Digimon must have 16000 DP at the time this card's effect is activated for it to gain ＜Blocker＞, ＜Reboot＞, and ＜Security A. +1＞.",
        "question": "I use this card's effect to give a Digimon +3000 DP, but it still has less than 16000 DP. If I then use another DP-boosting effect to raise its DP to 16000 or more, does it gain ＜Blocker＞, ＜Reboot＞, and ＜Security A. +1＞?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
